[
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a monad StateT + WriteT monad whose purpose is to track information about a mutually recursive function, and in principle equipping a function's type with it shouldn't change its behaviour at all. So I'm trying to replace <code>return</code> with a monadic function that logs information before returning:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ret_impl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Name</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Σ</span><span class=\"n\">ar</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LuaRepr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ar</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PartToLuaRepr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">tell</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">preReturn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Dynamic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">modify</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pred</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- add `scoped` eventually</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ret_impl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl_name</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, this doesn't have any effect and <code>#print</code>ing the definition of a function using <code>return</code> shows that <code>macro_rules</code> did not work. Would anyone know how to properly do this?</p>",
        "id": 580829174,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1774107774
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>is the <code>macro_rules</code> specifically targeting <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Parser.Term.doReturn#doc\">docs#Lean.Parser.Term.doReturn</a></p>",
        "id": 580829391,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1774107922
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is equivalent to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But you don't want to have a <code>term</code>, you want to have a <code>doElem</code>.</p>",
        "id": 580829504,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1774107999
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah I see, the following worked, thank you!</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ret_return</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">doElem</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">doElem</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">ret_impl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decl_name</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ret_return</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580829685,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1774108124
    }
]